From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm latent: the head block takes the head count back (test-cuda-host green)

The era rule is `headBlock(rows, heads)`: wide at 2048+ rows, or from 5 rows when heads
is 17-24 (TP=3's 22/21/21). The port had flattened it to `headBlock(rows)` with a 64-row
threshold, so a 22-head pass at rows 5..63 took the 16-head tile everywhere that rule is
read. `cuda_mla_ovn_test` caught the visible half: its sparse pass at 63 rows emitted
chunks_32_fp8 where the test expects chunks_32_fp8_skip (measured ids 51,46,50,46
against 51,46,51,46).

`latent.headBlockOf(rows, heads)` restores the rule and every read site uses it: the
sparse dispatch, the two dense/mixed sites in `cuda_dsa_block.zig` (which would
otherwise run 16-head chunks on the dense half and 32-head on the sparse half, writing
the same partials with different block counts), and `onepass.takesExact`. With the rule
uniform, the onepass test's five-row floor is correct again and its two adapted
expectations return to the era values, and `headBlockOf` gains two unit assertions
(8 rows/22 heads wide, 2 rows/22 heads tile).

Separately, 0022 moved the stepped pass into `cuda_lanes_step.zig`, which calls
`Leader.chunkOf`; the pin's `prefill_widths_glm_host.zig` stub declared `chunk` only and
stopped compiling. The stub gains `chunkOf` delegating to `chunk`, cap ignored.

Gates on pin+0001..0031: check-native-cuda-host green, whole-tree fmt green, lean
base-vs-head 0 new, and `test-cuda-host` exits 0 with zero named failures - the same
result a clean 9c9bf542 checkout gives, from 27 named failures at 0001..0023.

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- cuda_dsa_block.zig, cuda_latent.zig and cuda_onepass.zig apply as the fold has them; the prefill_widths_glm_host stub's chunkOf (the fold's reply-prefill hunk) is not needed: Lanes.prefillStep still calls Leader.chunk at v1.2.7.
- source: work/fold/0029-head-block-rule.patch

